# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_1000011> (cleavage period)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_1000011> "The period that immediately follows fertilization. It is characterized by rapid, synchronous mitotic cell divisions in the absence of cell growth. This period culminates in the formation of a hollow, spherical, multicellular, monolayered embryo (a blastula) with a hollow cavity (the blastocoel) in the center.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002175> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_1000011> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_46514>)
