# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000103> (animal pole)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000103> "The most apical region of the animal hemisphere. Among echinoderms, in euechinoids, it is characterized by the presence of long, immotile cilia constituting the apical tuft initially and then, in all echinoderms, by te presence of the oral hood and where the serotonergic neurons form.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002175> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000103> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_46514>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002175> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000103> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_7632>)
