# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000113> (hyaline layer)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000113> "A multilayered extraembryonic matrix that functions as a substrate for cell adhesion through early development. It forms initially from molecules secreted from cortical granules at fertilization and is modified through the secretion of additional material during later development. The principal component of the hyaline layer is the protein, hyalin.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002175> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000113> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_46514>)
