# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000120> (long immotile cilium)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000120> "A cilium of long size that does not contain molecular motors and as such does not exhibit any beating movement. In some echinoderms, long immotile cilia are found, when present, at the animal pole of embryos and constitute the apical tuft.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002175> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000120> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_46514>)
