# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000498> (blastopore lip)

AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000498> "The margin (or edge) of the blastopore. In echinoderms, it is the circular rim of the blastopore and the transition zone between the invaginated archenteron and the outer epithelium of the embryo. Because cells move over the lip of the blastopore during echinoderm gastrulation, different populations of cells are located at the blastopore lip as gastrulation proceeds.")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002175> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECAO_2000498> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_46514>)
